<git_state>
Before you do git work, read the current branch and `git status` yourself.
Do not rely on the git snapshot from session start, because the user and other sessions change the repository after it.
</git_state>

<codegraph>
In a repository with a `.codegraph/` folder at the root, use CodeGraph before `grep`, `find`, or a file read when you look for code or try to understand it, because CodeGraph also follows the calls that a text search cannot find, such as dynamic dispatch.
Run `codegraph explore "<symbol names or question>"`.
It gives the source of the related symbols with line numbers, and the call paths between them.
In a repository without `.codegraph/`, run `codegraph init -y` only when a dotclaude note tells you to.
</codegraph>

<project_commands>
The `CLAUDE.md`, `README.md`, and build files of a repository define its commands.
When a repository has no test or build command, say so in the report.
</project_commands>
